command output · write a completion summary or tick something off as done\",\n      \"[`evidence-and-proof.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md)\",\n      \"What counts as proof, how a green run lies, what an honest close-out contains\"\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"index_sample\": [\n    [\n      \"[Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md)\",\n      \"Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"[Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md)\",\n      \"The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed.\"\n    ]\n  ]\n}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"trigger_count\": 10,\n  \"index_count\": 10,\n  \"trigger_sample\": [\n    [\n      \"Add a file, module, class, interface, option, layer, or dependency · write a spec or plan that adds one · generalize something that works · write \\\"flexible\\\", \\\"future-proof\\\", \\\"scalable\\\", \\\"extensible\\\", \\\"might need\\\", \\\"best practice\\\", \\\"while we're here\\\" · add a test beyond the coverage floor\",\n      \"[`prevent-overengineering.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md)\",\n      \"Whether this should exist at all, and at what size\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Touch a file outside the ask · fix something noticed in passing · change something else because it would make the fix easier · rename, reformat, or delete beyond the named area · deviate from an approved plan · decide what to do with the rest when part of the work is blocked · notice a defect, smell or stale comment outside the files in scope\",\n      \"[`scope-discipline.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md)\",\n      \"What is yours to change, and how to raise what isn't\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Say \\\"done\\\", \\\"works\\\", \\\"fixed\\\", \\\"passing\\\", \\\"no regressions\\\" · report a result · quote a number · act on a tool's or sub-agent's success report · close out a turn · report a file path or command output · write a completion summary or tick something off as done\",\n      \"[`evidence-and-proof.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md)\",\n      \"What counts as proof, how a green run lies, what an honest close-out contains\"\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"index_sample\": [\n    [\n      \"[Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md)\",\n      \"Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"[Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md)\",\n      \"The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed.\"\n    ]\n  ]\n}\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"jq '.derived.repo_rules | {trigger_count: (.trigger_rows|length), index_count: (.index_rows|length), trigger_sample: .trigger_rows[0:3], index_sample: .index_rows[0:2]}' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794559437417,"end":1794559438202}}}}
